event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":100,"item_id":"rs_08e717f2ebd3090b016aca1ba6b3788196b981a5fab248240d","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Planning server implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing a plain HTML server to handle form submissions with a post-redirect model, making it easily accessible without needing an API or browser JavaScript. I'll embed CSS within the server while keeping views separate. Testing should utilize the built-in spawn functionality to fetch and restart as needed. The server will support URL encoded requests and has a limit of around 1MB for bodies. I'll also consider error handling for cases like render 400 errors and set up tests in a temporary directory."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":101,"item_id":"rs_08e717f2ebd3090b016aca1ba6b3788196b981a5fab248240d","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Planning server implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing a plain HTML server to handle form submissions with a post-redirect model, making it easily accessible without needing an API or browser JavaScript. I'll embed CSS within the server while keeping views separate. Testing should utilize the built-in spawn functionality to fetch and restart as needed. The server will support URL encoded requests and has a limit of around 1MB for bodies. I'll also consider error handling for cases like render 400 errors and set up tests in a temporary directory."}}

